8958530,2024-05-08,Credit card,General-purpose credit card or charge card,Problem with a purchase shown on your statement,Credit card company isn't resolving a dispute about a purchase on your statement,"On XX/XX/year> I was online looking at XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX. I happened upon a website that sold them and I was trying to discover the cost of them because none was listed, the next step was to provide my credit card number. I thought that I would be brought to a checkout that I could decline if needed. I was never brought to a checkout and thought that nothing even went through since I received no email or any other information as to an order proceeding. I got a notification from capital one to approve the charge and I said no because my card was charged without my permission. I called the next day and was told that since I provided my number it would proceed and to call the merchant. I saw the charge of {$230.00} and {$79.00} and called the merchant on XX/XX/year> because I had not verified anything and I had never seen the cost. I was told the order could not be cancelled and could not be returned. I said there was no order because I authorized nothing and in fact, would not have authorized that purchase. This was when I filed a dispute with Capital One. In the coming weeks I did receive items and did not open them and would be happy to send them back. 

